{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The current best (config_037, 70.6%) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, but scgpt has not been tested in any configuration. Since RNA is the dominant signal source (RNA-only multiprofile achieves ~65% vs. image-only ~33%), the RNA encoder choice is a high-leverage axis. Config_008 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) directly parallels config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, 65.0%), changing only the RNA encoder. This cleanly isolates whether scgpt captures more predictive structure than scvi_n200. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, the gain could compound with multiprofile aggregation, weighted fusion, and ViT-L in a follow-up multimodal experiment. If it does not, an entire branch of the search space (all scgpt configurations) is effectively ruled out, saving future budget for other axes. This is preferred over testing scgpt directly in the full multimodal setting (e.g., config_049) because the simpler RNA-only comparison provides cleaner attribution, and over testing transformer aggregation in the multimodal setting (config_039) because transformer≈avgpool is already well-established from the RNA-only evidence."
}

